<title>USA: U.S. Restaurant FFO $0.56 vs $0.46.</title>
<headline>U.S. Restaurant FFO $0.56 vs $0.46.</headline>
<dateline>DALLAS 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. RESTAURANT PROPERTIES MASTER LP</p>
<p>			  GAAP Income for the:</p>
<p>					  ($000s)</p>
<p>							 Three Months Ended</p>
<p>								  March 31,</p>
<p>							   1997	  1996</p>
<p> Net Income					    1,952	1,323</p>
<p>Cash Available for Distribution Per Unit (a)</p>
<p>							    0.55	 0.46</p>
<p>Funds Generated From Operations Per Unit (a)</p>
<p>							    0.56	 0.46</p>
<p>(a)  Funds from Operations (FFO) uses the NAREIT definition of FFO (i.e., GAAP net income adding back depreciation and</p>
<p>amortization) divided by primary shares outstanding which includes the impact of options if they were exercised.  Average primary shares outstanding were 7,077,532 for 1997 and 4,903,008 for 1st quarter 1996.</p>
<p>Cash available for distribution (&quot;CAD&quot;) deletes from the numerator of the FFO calculation non cash revenues from net income (i.e. straight-line rent accounting), and the denominator reflects the average outstanding units on which distributions are actually paid. Actual shares outstanding were 6,913,766 versus 4,903,008 in 1st quarter 1996.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
